  "text": "For hotel-conversion studies in the **United States and Canada**, the following brands are commonly screened. The most relevant are usually **soft brands/collections**, because they let an existing hotel retain more of its architecture, design and identity.\n\n### Primary upper-upscale conversion brands\n\n| Parent company | Brands commonly considered | Typical fit |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio** | Independent boutique, historic, urban and resort properties. Marriott specifically positions these collections as an operating platform for independent hotels. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Hilton** | **Curio Collection by Hilton**, **Tapestry Collection by Hilton** | Curio generally suits more distinctive or higher-rated full-service assets; Tapestry can accommodate somewhat more streamlined properties. Both are currently classified by STR as upper upscale and actively target conversions. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/releases/hiltons-curio-and-tapestry-collections-celebrate-200th-hotel-milestones?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Hyatt** | **JdV by Hyatt**; sometimes **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** | JdV is appropriate for lifestyle and neighborhood-oriented hotels. Unbound is considered for more distinctive, higher-end properties, although its portfolio spans upper-upscale and luxury positioning and STR currently classifies it as luxury. ([hyatt.com](https://www.hyatt.com/development/ourbrands/theunboundcollectionbyhyatt?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Choice Hotels** | **Radisson Individuals by Choice** | Upper-upscale soft brand for independent, boutique and full-service hotels. ([choicehotelsdevelopment.com](https://www.choicehotelsdevelopment.com/news/choice-hotels-relaunches-radisson-individuals-as-part-of-its-portfolio-of-brands-MCGUOTHASSNZBF5OUH7E7UATMTII?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **BWH Hotels** | **WorldHotels Crafted**, **WorldHotels Elite** | Independent lifestyle, boutique, resort and established destination hotels seeking relatively flexible affiliation. Both are currently classified as upper upscale by STR. ([worldhotels.com](https://www.worldhotels.com/content/luxury-hotels/en_US/hotel-development/information.html?utm_source=openai)) |\n\n### Hard brands also considered for conversions\n\nDepending on the building’s guestrooms, public space, meeting facilities and renovation budget, conversion studies may also examine:\n\n- **Marriott, Sheraton, Westin and Renaissance**\n- **Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Canopy by Hilton and Embassy Suites by Hilton**\n- **Hyatt Regency, Hyatt Centric and Hyatt**\n- **Radisson Blu and Radisson RED**\n- **Wyndham Grand and Dolce Hotels & Resorts**\n- **Royal Sonesta**\n- **Sandman Signature**, particularly in Canada\n\nThese brands are classified in STR’s current upper-upscale segment, although their physical standards can make conversions substantially more capital-intensive than soft-brand affiliations. Embassy Suites, for example, generally requires an all-suite configuration, while conventional full-service brands may require extensive ballroom, restaurant, lounge and back-of-house improvements. ([costar.com](https://www.costar.com/products/str-benchmark/resources/guidelines/str-chain-scales))\n\n### Adjacent brands frequently included in the analysis\n\nAlthough STR currently places them outside the strict upper-upscale category, conversion studies often also compare:\n\n- **DoubleTree by Hilton**\n- **Delta Hotels by Marriott**\n- **voco, Crowne Plaza and Hotel Indigo**\n- **Wyndham**\n- **Sonesta Hotels**\n- **Outset Collection by Hilton**\n\nThese are generally classified as **upscale**, but they may offer lower conversion costs or more flexible physical requirements. ([costar.com](https://www.costar.com/products/str-benchmark/resources/guidelines/str-chain-scales))\n\n**Practical initial shortlist:** For a typical independent full-service hotel, the first brands usually contacted are **Autograph, Tribute, Curio, Tapestry, JdV, Radisson Individuals and WorldHotels Crafted/Elite**, followed by the applicable hard brands based on layout, market position and required property-improvement plan. STR’s chain-scale assignments are ADR-based and are updated periodically, so they should be confirmed at the time of a specific feasibility or appraisal assignment. ([costar.com](https://www.costar.com/products/str-benchmark/resources/guidelines/str-chain-scales?utm_source=openai))",
